// House cleaning page, rebuilt from the SECOND revision of the Regular House
// Cleaning brief. Section choices, positioning, and every "don't invent this"
// call trace back to content-plans/home-cleaning.md — see its "Open items"
// list for everything flagged below.
//
// Ships at /house-cleaning/ per the plan's §0 slug ruling; the plan file is
// named home-cleaning.md after the brief's own title, not after the slug.
//
// WHAT THE SECOND BRIEF CHANGED, in one place:
//  1. ✅ Trust bar moves to the five points deep-cleaning.astro and
//     index.astro already carry. That closes deep-cleaning's own flag naming
//     this page as one of four still behind.
//  2. ✅ NEW §6 "Weekly, fortnightly or monthly" — a real 3×3 comparison
//     grid, ComparisonTable's exact contract.
//  3. ✅ NEW §8 "What you're actually buying" REPLACES the old "Nobody leaves
//     a cleaner over the cleaning" bullet block. Don't re-add the bullets.
//  4. ✅ NEW §11 "Easy to book, instant pricing, cost effective" — identical
//     to the section already shipping on deep-cleaning.astro.
//  5. ✅ "Where we clean" grows from a 12-town flat list to the same 56 towns
//     in three labelled groups deep-cleaning uses. Two stale
//     `isHighlighted` flags go with it — that property no longer exists on
//     TagCloud's Tag interface and astro check does not catch it.
//  6. ✅ FAQs go from 6 across two blocks to 12 in ONE accordion, including
//     the three the first build held back. Same [CONFIRM] handling
//     deep-cleaning established: strip the marker, flag inline, ship.
//  7. ✅ The closing block gets real copy, so the hero-echo placeholder goes.
//  8. ✅ §9's before/after gallery becomes a DRAGGABLE COMPARISON SLIDER
//     (the new BeforeAfter.astro), closing the first build's own flag that
//     nothing in this library paired two images as one unit. Wired to SAMPLE
//     illustrations for now — see the §9 block for the swap and the brief.
//  9. ❌ The old brief's "how we compare" table is gone from this revision
//     entirely. Closed, not deferred.
//
// Sections blocked on content that doesn't exist yet are built as RESERVED
// SLOTS — labelled Placeholder frames and bracketed [TBC] briefing text.
// Obviously unfinished on sight, zero layout shift when the real assets and
// quotes land. Never fill a reserved slot with invented photos, quotes or
// names — those are outward-facing trust claims, not filler.
